@BookService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5203

### Paged + sorted list
GET {{BookService_HostAddress}}/api/books?page=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=title&sortDir=asc
Accept: application/json

###

POST {{BookService_HostAddress}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Pragmatic Programmer",
  "author": "Andrew Hunt",
  "isbn": "9780201616224",
  "publishedYear": 1999,
  "category": "Programming",
  "totalCopies": 2,
  "availableCopies": 2
}

### CSV import
POST {{BookService_HostAddress}}/api/books/import/csv
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="books.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

Title,Author,Isbn,Category,TotalCopies,InventoryNumber,Barcode
Refactoring,Martin Fowler,9780201485677,Programming,2,INV-REF-001,BC-REF-001
--boundary--

### XML import
POST {{BookService_HostAddress}}/api/books/import/xml
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="books.xml"
Content-Type: application/xml

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<books>
  <book>
    <title>Working Effectively with Legacy Code</title>
    <author>Michael Feathers</author>
    <isbn>9780131177055</isbn>
    <publishedYear>2004</publishedYear>
    <category>Programming</category>
    <totalCopies>1</totalCopies>
    <inventoryNumber>INV-LEG-001</inventoryNumber>
    <barcode>BC-LEG-001</barcode>
  </book>
</books>
--boundary--

###
GET {{BookService_HostAddress}}/health

